body:
If there is no window manager running, detectEWMH returns without releasing the X11 error handler. The assert can be visible with test tools such as triangle-vulkan, window...

I tested it with an Xfce4 desktop and killing xfwm4 (with no restart).

OS and version: Red Hat Enterprise Linux release 8.6
Release or commit: glfw-3.4

Error messages:

build/tests $ triangle-vulkan
triangle-vulkan: /home/test/Downloads/glfw-3.4/glfw-3.4/src/x11_init.c:1099: _glfwGrabErrorHandlerX11: Assertion `_glfw.x11.errorHandler == NULL' failed.
Aborted (core dumped)

Call stack:

#0  __GI_raise (sig=sig@entry=6) at ../sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/raise.c:50
#1  0x00007ffff63c2db5 in __GI_abort () at abort.c:79
#2  0x00007ffff63c2c89 in __assert_fail_base (fmt=0x7ffff652b898 "%s%s%s:%u: %s%sAssertion `%s' failed.\n%n", 
    assertion=0x2023b50 "_glfw.x11.errorHandler == NULL", 
    file=0x2023b18 "/home/test/Downloads/glfw-3.4/glfw-3.4/src/x11_init.c", line=1099, function=<optimized out>)
    at assert.c:92
#3  0x00007ffff63e83a6 in __GI___assert_fail (assertion=0x2023b50 "_glfw.x11.errorHandler == NULL", 
    file=0x2023b18 "/home/test/Downloads/glfw-3.4/glfw-3.4/src/x11_init.c", line=1099, 
    function=0x2024240 <__PRETTY_FUNCTION__.17056> "_glfwGrabErrorHandlerX11") at assert.c:101
#4  0x00000000013fca06 in _glfwGrabErrorHandlerX11 ()
#5  0x00000000014013c9 in createNativeWindow ()
#6  0x0000000001404801 in _glfwCreateWindowX11 ()
#7  0x00000000013f47f7 in glfwCreateWindow ()

In x11_init.c around line 512:
```c
// Check whether the running window manager is EWMH-compliant
//
static void detectEWMH(void)
{
    // First we read the _NET_SUPPORTING_WM_CHECK property on the root window

    Window* windowFromRoot = NULL;
    if (!_glfwGetWindowPropertyX11(_glfw.x11.root,
                                   _glfw.x11.NET_SUPPORTING_WM_CHECK,
                                   XA_WINDOW,
                                   (unsigned char**) &windowFromRoot))
    {
        return;
    }

    _glfwGrabErrorHandlerX11();

    // If it exists, it should be the XID of a top-level window
    // Then we look for the same property on that window

    Window* windowFromChild = NULL;
    if (!_glfwGetWindowPropertyX11(*windowFromRoot,
                                   _glfw.x11.NET_SUPPORTING_WM_CHECK,
                                   XA_WINDOW,
                                   (unsigned char**) &windowFromChild))
    {
        --> missign this --> _glfwReleaseErrorHandlerX11();
        XFree(windowFromRoot);
        return;
    }

    _glfwReleaseErrorHandlerX11();

    // If the property exists, it should contain the XID of the window

...
```
I have added a line at 538 marked as "--> missing this -->".

Adding  _glfwReleaseErrorHandlerX11 there fix the assert and everything seems to work fine.
